@startuml BackendModuleStructure_Descriptive

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam noteBorderColor gray
skinparam noteBackgroundColor lightyellow

title Backend Module Structure of Human Benchmark

' Define layers as components
component "API Layer" as API #MistyRose
component "Application Layer" as APP #PaleGreen
component "Domain Layer" as DOM #LightBlue
component "Infrastructure Layer" as INF #Thistle
component "Shared Layer" as SH #LightGray

' Layout direction
top to bottom direction

' Dependencies (illustrative arrows)
API --> APP : calls business logic
APP --> DOM : operates on domain models
APP --> SH : uses helpers
DOM --> SH : uses shared contracts/utilities
APP --> INF : uses infrastructure services
INF --> SH : uses shared utilities

' Notes for each layer
note right of API
<b>API Layer</b>
- Controllers: RESTful HTTP endpoints  
- Hubs: WebSocket/SignalR communication  
- Filters: Auth, validation, etc.  
- DTOs: Request/response schemas
end note

note right of APP
<b>Application Layer</b>
- Services: Implements business logic  
- Commands/Queries: CQRS pattern  
- EventHandlers: React to domain events  
- Validators: Input checking
end note

note right of DOM
<b>Domain Layer</b>
- Entities: Core domain models  
- ValueObjects: Immutable types  
- DomainEvents: Triggered changes  
- Interfaces: Abstractions and contracts
end note

note right of INF
<b>Infrastructure Layer</b>
- Persistence: EF Core & DB access  
- Authentication: User auth services  
- ExternalServices: 3rd party integration  
- Logging: Backend log system
end note

note right of SH
<b>Shared Layer</b>
- Constants: System-wide enums  
- Extensions: Utility functions  
- Helpers: Common helpers/utilities
end note

@enduml
